<title>USA: Vestcom IPO over-allotment option exercised.</title>
<headline>Vestcom IPO over-allotment option exercised.</headline>
<dateline>LYNDHURST, N.J. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vestcom International Inc said on Tuesday that the managing underwriters of its initial public offering exercised in full an option to buy an additional 577,500 shares to cover over-allotment.</p>
<p>That brings the total number of shares offered to 4,427,500. The price to the public is $13 per share, the company said in a news release.</p>
<p>Vestcom is being formed to provide computer output and document management services.</p>
</text>
